<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52627" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλι-γένεια</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bearer of a fair
			offspring</i>, name by which Demeter was invoked in the
			Thesmophoria, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				299
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				2.4
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.205
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Acrae</span>); or her nurse, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>; epith. of the Moon, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hymn.Mag.</u>
				5.31
			</span></i>; of the Earth, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>:—neut. pl., <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καλλιγένεια</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύειν</span> offer <i>sacrifice to
				Demeter K.</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				3.39
			</span></i> (nisi leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ
		Κ.</span>).</div>
